# V1a: the single-card byte gate under the WATCHER (NoC sanitiser, waypoints) on a reduced scope: the helper's remote write into the owner's O ring and the
# owner's semaphore wait are exactly what the watcher checks. One card, a 1x1 mesh, four users x 16 rows at the four-card geometry; K5-A against V5 over R1
# (seed 17), the column-asymmetric RA and the controls. A reduced scope never reads PASS (exit 4 / NO-DECISION): this pass is for a watcher error, a hang and a
# first sight of any differing byte, not for the licence.
# Duration (estimate): 20-40 min (container timeout 3 h; a hang trips the per-call watchdog, exit 3, then reset the target card only).
# Read: no watcher error or assert line; the GDN_V5 verdict line; any FAIL names the first differing (user, head, token, tile, half). STOP on a watcher error, a hang or a FAIL.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/v5split window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/v5split and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is
# pushed from this branch.
# TWO IMAGES: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1 (a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes) is the build the single-card byte gate runs in (the gate mounts this
# checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs); C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2 is the build of the commit that adds the
# qualified sha256 triple (gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED), which the four-card jobs serve. A reused tag is skipped by the build step.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/v5split/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--sections selftest,p0,negative --regimes R1,RA --seeds 17 --other-seeds 17
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1 WATCHER=1 HF_CACHE=/home/thatch/hf-cache
